  "question": {
    "text": "A magnetic needle of magnetic moment <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mo>.7</mo><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math> and moment of inertia <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>7</mn><mo>.5</mo><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math> is performing simple harmonic oscillations in a magnetic field of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>01</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></math>. Time taken for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn></math> complete oscillations is:",
